# Green p1 task 1.13 (remediation round 2)

The committed Red change d632534 (tests) and 885947e (plan) sit inside
phase_base_sha..HEAD. HEAD at start was 885947e176c9ce5f6d63f836aabbb0dbc99867c8,
the role_base_sha. Dirty paths .opencode/ and tech-debt.md were not touched.

Fixes (all in harness/model-guide/):

- preview.sh: resolves --export and --preview against the caller folder
  before any cd, and uses only absolute paths after that (F12, F14).
  A flag as the last argument or an empty --export / --preview value gives
  the usage line on stderr, exit 2, stdout empty, no write (F15).
  The root path / gives `preview: refused path /`, exit 2, before any tool
  starts (F20). The header names the `preview: refused path` refusal (F19).
  The docs/ copy runs before real-work.ts, so the fresh real-work.json and
  real-work.html win over stale docs copies (F13). A refused input check
  removes the preview folder when the run created it, so no new preview
  folder remains (F19).
- real-work.ts: each coverage key that preview.sh reads is required in the
  schema check. A missing key gives `input-check: schema`, exit 2, before
  any write (F17).
- publish.ts: a malformed approval row gives `publish: bad line <text>`,
  exit 2, stderr empty, no copy (F16). A record path that names a folder
  gives `publish: bad path <path>`, exit 2 (F18). The drift set uses
  own-property checks, so a docs file named constructor or toString is
  flagged (F23). Invalid preview-base JSON gives `publish: bad preview
  base`, exit 2, stderr empty, no stack trace (F23).
- F21: the task 1.9 preview command re-ran once at the final code HEAD
  (default preview folder). See preview-1.13.txt. Exit 0; the page shows
  the pinned SHA-256, generated_on, runs, date range, and shares.
  `git status --short docs/` prints nothing. No real export byte entered
  the repo.

Brief vs tests: no difference. The tests are the source of truth for the
exact refusal texts and were followed.

